-- examples/checks/agg-label-cap-check.rofl — agg_label_cap over
-- agg-label-cap-data.rofl (docs/aggregates.md, "Labeled unknowns", the cap):
-- g1 holds k9, and five members (lc5) or two (lc2) are in groups not known.
-- The five unknowns could each be told apart by g1 or by the class of the
-- rest, in any sharing among them: 203 regions of one group, past the cap of
-- 64, so the count of g1 is not decided by them and its shrug says how many
-- there were; the two make 5 and are no cap. g1 is a shrug in both, as no
-- completion count agrees (1 to 3 for two, 1 to 6 for five). The total over
-- all groups is what the members are, 3 for two (the group of each is where
-- it adds one) and, for five, a shrug: g1's count is the cap's.
alarm(lcap_wrong).
lcap(K, N, L) :- shrug(_, budget, spent(K, N, L)).
lc_sh2(G) :- shrug(lc2c(G, _), _, _).
lc_sh5(G) :- shrug(lc5c(G, _), _, _).
-- expect-row: lcap[main](regions,203,64)
-- expect-no-row: lcap[main](regions,5,
-- expect-row: lc_sh2[main](g1)
-- expect-row: lc_sh5[main](g1)
-- expect-no-row: lc2c[main](g1,
-- expect-no-row: lc5c[main](g1,
-- expect-row: lc2tot[main](3)
-- expect-no-row: lc5tot[main](
